  "inbox_items": [
    {
      "ref": "01KFH76C",
      "text": "Cross-feature requirement pattern: How to express that core features (search, validate, export) must support all entity types. When new entity type added, should automatically imply tasks for core features. Options: (1) applies_to field on feature specs, (2) trait on entity types like @trait-searchable, (3) validation warning for missing coverage, (4) parent spec that entity types must satisfy. Surfaced when realizing search doesn't cover inbox.",
      "created_at": "2026-01-21T21:25:59.163Z",
      "tags": [
        "design",
        "spec-model",
        "meta"
      ],
      "added_by": "@claude",
      "triaged": true,
      "triage_action": "spec-gap"
    },
    {
      "ref": "01KFHJNZ",
      "text": "Reverse spec lookup - kspec which <file> or kspec which <file:line> to find specs/ACs that reference or are implemented by a given code path. Useful for bug fixes to quickly discover what specs need updating. Could scan for // AC: annotations and spec_ref links. Instructive, helps find already-instrumented code.",
      "created_at": "2026-01-22T00:46:44.345Z",
      "tags": [
        "dx",
        "tooling",
        "reflection"
      ],
      "added_by": "@claude",
      "triaged": true,
      "triage_action": "defer"
    },
    {
      "ref": "01KFPDCY",
      "text": "Add cross-platform CI matrix testing - run core functionality tests on Windows, macOS, and Linux. Would catch issues like Unix-specific commands (which, cp -r) before they reach PR review. Consider: matrix strategy in GitHub Actions, platform-specific test skips where needed, focus on CLI commands and daemon lifecycle.",
      "created_at": "2026-01-23T21:50:37.263Z",
      "tags": [
        "ci",
        "testing",
        "dx"
      ],
      "added_by": "@claude",
      "triaged": true,
      "triage_action": "defer"
    },
    {
      "ref": "01KFQ517",
      "text": "E2E tests: Use isolated port range (not 3456) + cross-platform cleanup. Current approach conflicts with existing daemons. Should use high ephemeral port range and improve cleanup mechanism.",
      "created_at": "2026-01-24T04:43:39.058Z",
      "tags": [
        "e2e",
        "testing",
        "reflection"
      ],
      "added_by": "@claude",
      "triaged": true,
      "triage_action": "defer"
    },
    {
      "ref": "01KFYAHF",
      "text": "E2E test dev mode - configure Playwright to work with vite dev server instead of requiring full build for faster test iteration (12+ seconds to 1-2 seconds)",
      "created_at": "2026-01-26T23:34:35.746Z",
      "tags": [
        "e2e",
        "dx"
      ],
      "added_by": "@claude",
      "triaged": true,
      "triage_action": "defer"
    },
    {
      "ref": "01KGG6GY",
      "text": "Improve derive granularity: Research suggests specs with 4+ ACs are candidates for splitting. Potential enhancements: (1) --by-ac flag to create tasks per AC group, (2) --max-acs N to auto-group, (3) implementation_phases field in specs, (4) derive templates for common patterns (cli-command, api-endpoint), (5) complexity warnings when specs are too large. See session research on task decomposition patterns from Linear, Atlassian, BDD/Example Mapping, and AI coding assistants.",
      "created_at": "2026-02-02T22:10:44.331Z",
      "tags": [],
      "added_by": "@claude",
      "triaged": true,
      "triage_action": "defer"
    },
    {
      "ref": "01KGGEMM",
      "text": "Daemon debugging improvements: (1) Add --log-file or --verbose to 'kspec serve start', (2) Log resolved web UI path on startup, (3) Capture and show stderr when daemon fails to start within timeout. Consolidated from @01KFQ586, @01KFQ595, @01KFPH3D.",
      "created_at": "2026-02-03T00:32:32.926Z",
      "tags": [
        "daemon",
        "dx",
        "deferred"
      ],
      "added_by": "@claude",
      "triaged": true,
      "triage_action": "defer"
    },
    {
      "ref": "01KGGF4Y",
      "text": "Project config file (kspec.config.yaml or .kspecrc): Configure shadow remote URL (enable separate repo for specs), feature toggles, default values (author, priority), validation strictness. Enables multi-repo projects sharing specs and tailoring kspec to project needs. Consolidated from @01KFGVVJ, @01KFGVVN.",
      "created_at": "2026-02-03T00:41:28.272Z",
      "tags": [
        "feature",
        "config",
        "dx",
        "deferred"
      ],
      "added_by": "@claude",
